{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-hecke-operations-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:hecke-operations-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 2 from rem:hecke-operations","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hecke-operations"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"hecke-operations-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:hecke-operations-table2-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Table 2 from rem:hecke-operations</em></p>\n<p>The rows trace the confinement build-up of the gluon unit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1}</code>: squaring and then cubing it drives net<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q_0)</code> from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.791</code> through <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.800</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+1.000</code>, so the cubed operation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^3 = B_3</code> is the full-Borromean confinement fixed point.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n<th align=\"center\">net<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q_0)</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1}</code> (gluon unit)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-h_{\\mathrm{A}}\\cdot\\sigma_0 + L_+</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.791</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^2</code></td>\n<td>Intermediate Borromean (5 terms)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.800</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^3 = B_3</code></td>\n<td>Full Borromean confinement (5 terms)</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+1.000</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
